<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>9.10.7: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02508</md:content-id>
    <md:title>9.10.7: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>e604e538-5c73-4d6b-b90a-c2361fb84f54</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<section class="check-understanding"><exercise id="_8c25877c-9dbc-44e7-861f-f5cf0ed3b65f" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Select three statements that are true about the graph of this function.</para><para>The following quadratic expressions all define the same function.</para>
      <para> \((x+5)(x+3)\) </para>
        <para> \(x^2+8x+15\) </para>
        <para> \((x+4)^2−1\) </para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! The vertex is \((-4,-1)\), the \(x\)-intercepts are \((-5,0)\) and \((-3,0)\), the \(y\)-intercept is \((0,15)\).</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.10.1. </para><para>The correct answers are: The vertex is \((-4,-1)\), the \(x\)-intercepts are \((-5,0)\) and \((-3,0)\), the \(y\)-intercept is \((0,15)\). </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="d1b254ae-9370-478e-a72b-d731b6830440" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Enter the value of the \(y\)-coordinate.</para><para>The following expressions all define the same quadratic function.</para>
      <para> \((x−4)(x+6)\) </para>
        <para> \(x^2+2x−24\) </para>
        <para> \((x+1)^2−25\) </para>
      <para>What is the value of the \(y\)-coordinate of the \(y\)-intercept \((0, \_\_\_)\) of the graph of the function?</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! The \(y\)-intercept is \((0,-24)\).</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.10.1. </para><para>The correct answer is -24. The \(y\)-intercept is \((0,-24)\).
      </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="bbf0723e-dd5f-4632-8aaf-6419c4973eec" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para><emphasis>Select two</emphasis> \(x\)-intercepts of the graph.</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! The \(x\)-intercepts of the graph are \((-6,0)\) and \((4,0)\).</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.10.1. </para><para>The correct answers are: \((-6,0)\), \((4,0)\). The \(x\)-intercepts of the graph are \((-6,0)\) and \((4,0)\). </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_8868d88b-2575-4438-9a84-f97e79918f49" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Enter the \(x\)-coordinate.</para><para>What is the \(x\)-coordinate of the vertex of the graph?</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! The \(x\)-coordinate of the vertex of the graph is -1.</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 9.10.1 and 9.10.6. </para><para>The correct answer is -1. The \(x\)-coordinate of the vertex of the graph is -1. </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="e8df213e-14b1-4b54-8b38-fe140f2a3865" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Enter the \(y\)-coordinate.</para><para>What is the \(y\)-coordinate of the vertex of the graph?</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! The \(y\)-coordinate of the vertex of the graph is -25.</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 9.10.1 and 9.10.6. </para><para>The correct answer is -25. The \(y\)-coordinate of the vertex graph is -25.
      </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="faee25e1-e05c-447b-b41d-a7a8cb448a5f" class="multiple-choice"><problem><newline/><para>Is this an accurate graph of the function?</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! Yes. The \(x\)-intercepts, \(y\)-intercept, and vertex are plotted accurately.</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 9.10.1 and 9.10.6. </para><para>The correct answer is Yes. The \(x\)-intercepts, \(y\)-intercept, and vertex are plotted accurately. </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_023b0c87-8a26-40f5-822f-bc7e5d89c329" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Original expression
        \(x^2−7x+6\)</para><para>Here is one way an expression in standard form is rewritten into vertex form.</para>
      <para><emphasis>Step 1</emphasis> - \(x^2−7x+(-\frac{7}{2})^2+6−(-\frac{7}{2})^2\)</para>
      <para><emphasis>Step 2</emphasis> - \((x−\frac{7}{2})^2+6−\frac{49}{4}\)</para>
      <para><emphasis>Step 3</emphasis> - \((x−\frac{7}{2})^2+\frac{24}{4}−\frac{49}{4}\)</para>
      <para><emphasis>Step 4</emphasis> - \((x−\frac{7}{2})^2-\frac{25}{4}\)</para>
      <para>In Step 1, where did the number \(-\frac{7}{2}\) come from?</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>It is the substitute value for \(x\).</para><para>Every term in the expression was divided by 2.</para><para>It is half of -7 being squared.</para><para>Only the non-linear term was divided by 2.</para></problem><solution><para>Correct! It is half of -7 being squared.</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.10.3. </para><para>The correct answer is: It is half of -7 being squared. </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="f4e40af1-4c16-4820-9742-55da706419ba" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>In Step 1, why was \((-\frac{7}{2})^2\) added and then subtracted?</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>It is added to complete the square. It is subtracted to keep the value of the expression unchanged.</para><para>It is subtracted to complete the square. It is added to keep the value of the expression unchanged. </para><para>It is added to complete the square. It is subtracted to change the value of the expression.</para><para>It is subtracted to complete the square. It is added to change the value of the expression.</para></problem><solution><para>Correct! It is added to complete the square. It is subtracted to keep the value of the expression unchanged.</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.10.3. </para><para>The correct answer is: It is added to complete the square. It is subtracted to keep the value of the expression unchanged. </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="a9cb3566-dd50-4111-9c3d-4dd33e0f0626" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>What happened in Step 2?</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>The expression is subtracted to keep the value of the expression unchanged.</para><para>The expression, which is a perfect square, is written as a squared expression.</para><para>The expression, which is not a perfect square, is written as a squared expression.</para><para>The expression is added to keep the value of the expression unchanged.</para></problem><solution><para>Correct! The expression, which is a perfect square, is written as a squared expression. </para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.10.3. </para><para>The correct answer is: The expression, which is a perfect square, is written as a squared expression. </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_953b3ef1-2fe4-4336-945a-ca2aedee3adb" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>What happened in Step 3?</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>The quadratic term is written as a fraction so that it has a common denominator, which makes it easier to subtract. </para><para>A random term was added to complete the square.</para><para>The linear term is written as a fraction so that it has a common denominator, which makes it easier to subtract.</para><para>The constant term is written as a fraction so that it has a common denominator, which makes it easier to subtract.</para></problem><solution><para>Correct! The constant term is written as a fraction so that it has a common denominator, which makes it easier to subtract.</para><para> Try again. Revisit activity 9.10.3. </para><para>The correct answer is: The constant term is written as a fraction so that it has a common denominator, which makes it easier to subtract. </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="a043e713-3976-41a1-85a5-ba0bbb4f8b11" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>What does the last expression tell us about the vertex of the graph of a function defined by this expression?</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>The vertex of the graph is at \((-6\frac{1}{4}, \frac{7}{2})\).</para><para>The vertex of the graph is at \((\frac{5}{2}, -\frac{5}{2})\).</para><para>The vertex of the graph is at \((\frac{7}{2}, -6\frac{1}{4})\).</para><para>The vertex of the graph is at \((\frac{5}{2}, -6)\).</para></problem><solution><para>Correct! The vertex of the graph is at \((\frac{7}{2}, -6\frac{1}{4})\).</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 9.10.3 and 9.10.6. </para><para>The correct answer is: The vertex of the graph is at \((\frac{7}{2}, -6\frac{1}{4})\).
      </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_9c95eec7-1f50-47b2-b4a7-9799d8a2f05e" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\(d(x)=(x\_\_\_)^2\).</para><para>Enter the missing number, including the sign, for the expression when \(d(x)=x^2+12x+36\) is written in vertex form.</para>
      <para> Enter the missing number, including the sign.</para>
    </problem><solution><para>Correct! +6</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.10.3. </para><para>The correct answer is +6.
      </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_1a5fdedf-1462-4fae-bd8b-d5949c15dbcc" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Enter the missing number, including the sign.</para><para>Enter the missing numbers, including the signs, for the expression when \(f(x)=x^2+10x+21\) is written in vertex form. \(f(x)=(x + \underline{\;\mathbf a\boldsymbol.\;})^2 \underline{\;\mathbf b\boldsymbol.\;}\)</para>
      <para>What is the value of the missing number, including the sign, in the place of the letter a?
        </para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! +5</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.10.3. </para><para>The correct answer is +5. </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_017764f0-7d22-4926-a01a-0e8c8dfdd5a7" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Enter the missing number, including the sign.</para><para>What is the value of the missing number, including the sign, for the letter b?</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! -4</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.10.3. </para><para>The correct answer is -4.
      </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="a48a9b81-e218-4090-943c-5f7c96c157c4" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Enter the missing number, including the sign.</para><para>Enter the missing numbers, including the signs, for the expression when \(g(x)=2x^2−20x+32\) is written in vertex form. \(g(x)= \underline{\;\mathbf a\boldsymbol.\;} (x + \underline{\;\mathbf b\boldsymbol.\;} )^2 \underline{\;\mathbf c\boldsymbol.\;}\) </para>
      <para>What is the value of the missing number, including the sign, in place of letter a?</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! +2</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.10.4. </para><para>The correct answer is +2.
      </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_2308bf80-4901-486c-9dbe-19b42780bfb3" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Enter the missing number, including the sign.</para><para>What is the value of the missing number, including the sign, in place of letter b?</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! -5</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.10.4. </para><para>The correct answer is -5. </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_8afd5728-f7a1-47bf-a766-99de49fec590" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>What is the value of the missing number, including the sign, in place of letter c?</para>
        <para>Enter the missing number, including the sign. </para>
      </problem><solution><para> Correct! -18</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.10.4. </para><para>The correct answer is -18.
      </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="c9e197d5-fd93-42b2-aa5e-b5b594e38f64" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Enter the missing number, including the sign.</para><para>Enter the missing numbers, including the signs, for the expression when \(h(x)=(4x-3)^2\) is expanded to standard form. \(h(x)= ( \underline{\;\mathbf a\boldsymbol.\;}\; x )^2 + 2 ( \underline{\;\mathbf b\boldsymbol.\;}\; x)(-3) + ( \underline{\;\mathbf c\boldsymbol.\;} )^2\)</para>
      <para>What is the value of the missing number, including the sign, in place of letter a?</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! +16</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.10.2. </para><para>The correct answer is +16. </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="a55b2c00-d2fc-4e5a-a8f8-7e688b175331" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Enter the missing number, including the sign.</para><para>What is the value of the missing number, including the sign, in place of letter b?</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! -24</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.10.2. </para><para>The correct answer is -24.
      </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="abf63915-937f-4b57-89c4-027511d62d02" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Enter the missing number, including the sign.</para><para>What is the value of the missing number, including the sign, in place of letter c?</para>
      </problem><solution><para> Correct! +9</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 9.10.2. </para><para>The correct answer is +9. </para></solution></exercise></section></section>
